From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pet0203 <Pet0203@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mb/google/asurada: always bring the display up

Stock ChromeOS firmware initialises the display only when vboot asks for
it: recovery, developer mode, a diagnostics request, or the one-shot
VB2_NV_DISPLAY_REQUEST bit. A normal-mode boot asks for none of those, so
there is no panel and no framebuffer by the time the payload runs.

A firmware that prompts for a disk unlock PIN on every normal boot needs
one. depthcharge cannot make up for it: this board registers no DisplayOps,
so its display_init() prints "called but not implemented" and returns, and
a prompt drawn on a panel that was never powered looks exactly like a
machine that has died.

Call configure_display() unconditionally. It has to be done here rather
than by changing what vboot reports: that flag is decided in verstage,
which lives in the RO section behind the hardware write-protect, while
ramstage is in the RW section and can be replaced by an ordinary RW update.

Checked on spherion before writing this: setting VB2_NV_DISPLAY_REQUEST by
hand for a single boot (crossystem display_request=1) made coreboot log
"configure_display: Starting display init" and bring up the panel at
1920x1080. With this patch the same happens on every boot, with that bit
clear.

Cost: every normal boot pays for panel bring-up, whether or not anything
is drawn.
---
 src/mainboard/google/asurada/mainboard.c | 17 +++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/google/asurada/mainboard.c b/src/mainboard/google/asurada/mainboard.c
index 7704899f..bd988500 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/google/asurada/mainboard.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/google/asurada/mainboard.c
@@ -235,10 +235,19 @@ static void mainboard_init(struct device *dev)
 	if (spm_init())
 		printk(BIOS_ERR, "spm init fail, system suspend may stuck\n");
 
-	if (display_init_required())
-		configure_display();
-	else
-		printk(BIOS_INFO, "%s: Skipped display init\n", __func__);
+	/*
+	 * Unconditionally, not only when vboot asks for it. This firmware
+	 * prompts for a disk unlock PIN on every normal boot, and a prompt
+	 * drawn on a panel that was never powered is indistinguishable from a
+	 * machine that has died.
+	 *
+	 * The flag this used to test is decided in verstage, which lives in
+	 * the RO section behind the hardware write-protect, so it cannot be
+	 * changed without unprotecting the chip. ramstage is in the RW section
+	 * we sign and flash, so this is where the decision can still be made.
+	 */
+	if (!configure_display())
+		printk(BIOS_ERR, "%s: display init failed\n", __func__);
 }
 
 static void mainboard_enable(struct device *dev)
